# Midgard lore, myths and exploration talk (classic + Shrouded Isles, up to 1.65).
# Documented lore is said plainly; rumours, superstitions and inventions are said as belief, memory or argument.
# Named monsters are ones that live in this world. Lore only for the 70+ raid bosses: nobody here claims a kill.

@kind ambient
@realm mid
@topic lore
@about place

# ---------------- The hidden road: Odin's Gate, the sealed hall, the first city (explorers) ----------------
@who Explorer
@levels 15-50
they call it odin's gate. i have walked every hill of it and never found a gate
my grandfather swore the real road to asgard starts behind a waterfall. he never said which waterfall
an old map in our guild house shows a waterfall in gripklosa. i have never found it
the old skalds [say|claim] there is a sealed hall of the first gods [under the ice|beneath the glacier], [older than jordheim|older than any house in jordheim]
[heard|i heard] the bifrost [still stands|is still out there], [just|only] [hidden in the northern lights|folded up in the green lights]. pretty story anyway
swam north off the edge of the map once. the sea just kept going, but i swear i saw a wall of light out there
an old dwarf in jordheim told me the troll fathers built their first city under the ice, long before trollheim
trollheim is the troll fathers' second city, if the old stories are right. nobody can tell me where the first one went
every map of midgard ends at the [ice|sea], [but|and] [nobody|no one] [i know|ive met] has [walked|swum] to where it actually ends
yggdra forest is named for the world tree. then where is the tree. i have looked
[i keep|i still keep] a list of [caves|holes in the hills] nobody [talks about|ever mentions]. [its getting long|the list gets longer every week]
walked past a cave mouth in uppland for months before i noticed it. makes you wonder what else we all walk past
the world keeps finding islands. a few new ones turned up not long ago, so dont tell me the map is finished
aegir was a sailors' story too, once. then we all went there. think about that
if odin left a door [open|unlocked] somewhere, my bet is [under the glacier|behind the glacier giant]. why else would something that big just stand there
someone told me you can see the gods' hall from the highest peak in jamtland on a clear night. only saw clouds myself
some say the glacier giant isnt guarding the frontier, hes guarding a door. i half believe it
climbed as high as you can go in gripklosa once. nothing up there but wind, and a feeling somebody carved those ledges
the mountains around jordheim look carved if you stare long enough. the dwarves say the gods did it
i could swear there is a door in jordheim nobody uses. ive knocked. nothing
spindelhalla, trollheim, the iarnwood lair, the glacier. every one of them was a rumour first. so whats the next one
odin hung on the tree nine nights for the runes. [i think|my guess is] the tree is still out there, [roots down|growing] [under yggdra|beneath yggdra forest]
[found|i found] a rune carved on a rock in [myrkwood|gotar] that no runemaster [could|i asked could] read. [never found it again|went back and couldnt find the rock]
[the sea|the water] past aegirhamn goes black after a while. [i turned back|i swam back]. [not proud|no shame in it]
a guildmate swore he swam so far north the stars looked wrong. i half believe him
swam the length of munin sound once just to see where it ends. cramps stopped me before the map did
modernagrav wasnt on any map i owned a while back. now there is a whole island. whats next
[i like to think|i still believe] some of midgard [is still|was left] [unwalked|unmapped] [on purpose|for us to find]
the green lights over the north are the bifrost [folded up|shut tight], [an old seer told me|my grandmother used to say]. she never said who folded it

# The hidden road, said by veterans and the curious
@who NoLifer,Socialite
@levels 25-50
[back when i was new|when i started], [we|people] thought malmohus was the edge of the world. [funny|look at us] now
i remember when nobody knew what was across the water. everyone just told stories about it
[gossip|word] in jordheim is a hunter found a passage behind a waterfall in [gripklosa|munin sound]. [nobody can find it twice|he wont say where]
[gossip|the talk] in the taverns is that the dwarves of delling crater know the way to the sealed hall. [they just|they] [wont tell|smile and say nothing]
heard a troll in jordheim say his grandfather walked the first city under the ice. then he changed the subject

# ---------------- Gjalpinulva, the wolf-headed dragon of Malmohus ----------------
@who *
@levels 35-50
gjalpinulva is a daughter of the fenris wolf, which is why she looks the way she does
skona's werewolves wont set foot in malmohus. think about that
the drakulvs in malmohus were bred by the dragon. two legs, scales, wolf faces. nobody asked for that
[heard|someone told me] gjalpinulva talks to your corpse after she kills you. [never stuck around to listen|i always released too fast to hear]
rule one at the dragon: nobody nukes until the tanks have her, or we all eat the breath
[half the raid|my whole guild] calls gjalpinulva a he. the [old songs|skalds] say she. [i stopped|ive stopped] arguing about it
[people say|rumour is] the dragon goes berserk if you bring [too many|over a hundred]. [never tested it|no idea if its true]
the svartalfar [spy on|keep watch on] malmohus from the edges. [whatever they're waiting for|whatever they want], [its not good|i dont like it]
the dragon [drops|gives] [mostly|little more than] coin, [if you ask me|they say]. the luminescent stones are the real reason anyone goes
an old raid leader swore the drakulv soultrappers keep the souls of the dragon's dead. creepy if true
never say the dragon's name inside malmohus. its bad luck, my healer insists
malmohus is little known and less explored, said the old scouts. still true if you ask me
[i think|my guess is] the dragon under tuscaran was gjalpinulva's [mother|kin]. cant prove it, just how it feels
somewhere fenris is still chained. his daughter sits in malmohus, so lets hope the chain holds
[i keep a respec stone|keeping a luminescent stone] [for luck|in my bag], [from|out of] a dragon raid i [barely|only] watched from the hill

@who NoLifer
@levels 40-50
the first dragon raid i ever saw had more people than jordheim on a holiday. it lasted about three minutes
i remember watching our realm's first dragon raid form up outside jordheim. most of us never even reached malmohus
[the old raids|raids back then] [fought|stood] inside the ruins, because anyone [hitting|attacking] from outside [pulled|drew] the breath on everyone

@who Daredevil
@levels 40-50
one day im walking into malmohus alone just to see the dragon's face. tell my guild i was brave
[bet|i bet] nobody here has [tagged|touched] the dragon solo and walked out. [i want to be the first|i want to try]

# ---------------- The Glacier Giant of Odin's Gate ----------------
@who *
@levels 30-50
[the glacier giant|glacier giant] throws people. [like|i mean] [across the zone|half a mile], not a figure of speech
my old group used to bet on where people would land when the glacier giant threw them. best was near uppland
heard killing the glacier giant takes the fire out of the dragon. i think whoever said that was drunk
the glacier giant is the biggest thing in the world, i think. nobody ive met has seen a bigger one
got thrown by the glacier giant once and landed next to a hib stealther. we both just stood there
ran past the glacier giant at 20 once to see how close i could get. i got about ten steps

@who Daredevil
@levels 30-50
[dare|i dare] [anyone|someone] to stand still next to the glacier giant for ten seconds. [nobody has|no one ever has]

# ---------------- Gods and their houses (class trainers' lore) ----------------
@who *
@levels 5-50
@class Bonedancer
the house of bodgar is older than the other houses, whatever the priests of odin tell you
@class Spiritmaster
we serve the house of hel. [people|folk] get [nervous|quiet] when i say that out loud
@class Runemaster
the house of odin taught me every rune is a key. i still havent found what most of them open
@class Thane
the house of thor likes us loud. its in the oath, more or less
@class Healer
eir keeps the healers. nobody thanks her until the group lives
@class Hunter
skadi's house taught us to hunt in the snow. midgard has no shortage of cold
@class Shadowblade
the house of loki trains the shadowblades. never ask us where our god is tonight
@class Warrior
tyr gave his hand to the wolf. warriors remember that every time we step in front of a pull
@class Skald
bragi watches over the skalds. every saga i sing is half true and the rest is for the crowd
@class Berserker
the house of modi doesnt ask how many. only where
@class Shaman
shamans answer to the house of ymir. yes, that ymir. the giants' first father
@class Savage
kelgor's house says the body is the weapon. my healer disagrees every fight
@class *
the gods are still alive in midgard. the other realms just have old stories
always found it strange that bonedancers and the valkyn pray to the same bodgar
the valkyn pray to bodgar, a god of the dead older than odin himself, they say
the dwarves are the oldest race in midgard and they never let you forget it
kobolds are drawn to runes like moths to [a lamp|a fire]. [ask any runemaster|ask a runemaster why]
[sometimes|some nights] the sky over jordheim turns green. [the old ones|old folk] say [the gods are arguing|its the bifrost]
trolls came down out of the mountains to help us. no one remembers what they were doing up there first

# ---------------- Ragnarok ----------------
@levels 10-50
my guild leader swears ragnarok already happened and we live in the long afterward
if ragnarok ever comes i want to be 50 with my armor paid off
the fire giants in muspelheim are getting ready for ragnarok. thats what my dwarf healer says, anyway
[i figure|way i see it] ragnarok [cant|wont] start while [thor's hammer|the hammer] [sits|stays] in midgard. [so|which is why] we guard it
some say every realm war is just practice for ragnarok. i hope they are wrong

# ---------------- Giants: Muspelheim and Vanern ----------------
@levels 15-50
fire giants in muspelheim, jotuns in vanern, frost giants on the glacier. midgard is built on giants' quarrels
[the dverge|dverge] in muspelheim work the fires for the giants, [they say|i think]. [cant blame them for the attitude|they dont look happy about it]
the shade of gunnar walks muspelheim. [nobody|no one] [i know|ive asked] [knows|can say] who gunnar was
the clay jotuns in vanern were made by someone. clay doesnt walk on its own
one jotun outcast in vanern stared at me like he wanted to say something. then he swung
[i heard|so i heard] the jotuns of vanern still [pray to|remember] ymir, [quietly|when nobody is looking]
rottild the traitor lives out in vanern. [nobody|no one] [remembers|can tell me] who [she|rottild] betrayed

# ---------------- Spindelhalla and the other mainland dungeons ----------------
@levels 15-50
the arachites keep svartalf slaves in spindelhalla to tend the [spiders|silk]. [grim stuff|makes my skin crawl]
the arachite prelates in spindelhalla pray to something in the deep. never stayed to find out what
[old|some] [scouts|explorers] [say|claim] spindelhalla goes deeper than the maps. [the webs hide another stair|the silk covers the rest]
king hresvelgr rules the werewolves of varulvhamn. hresvelgr was a giant eagle in the old songs. nobody knows why a wolf took the name
[dont|never] whistle in vendo caverns. [something|grjotgard] [hears|answers], [my old group swore|everyone knows that]
the dread lichess in the cursed tomb was a queen once, they say. nobody says whose
nisse was a house spirit gone bad, my gran said. leave out porridge and he's harmless
i tap my shield three times before going into trollheim. laugh all you want, i keep coming back

# ---------------- Trollheim, the Troll Fathers, Nosdoden ----------------
@levels 30-50
nosdoden leaves an apparition of every adventurer he kills. rez your dead fast and it fades
[heard|they say] nosdoden was a [proper|true] dragon once, [before trollheim twisted him|before something down there changed him]
there is a bartender in trollheim. his name is olen. i have never been served
the troll fathers came before trolls and kobolds both. makes [you|me] look at [your|my] kobold [friends|groupmates] differently
trollheim has an up leader and a down leader, uppat and nedat. my troll friend swears it meant something holy once
[a troll|my troll friend] told me trollheim [still smells of|smells like] his grandfather. [i didnt ask further|didnt ask]
first time in trollheim we wandered for an hour. the halls just keep going down
[i think|my theory is] nosdoden's apparitions are what the troll fathers left behind. [ghosts of ghosts|nobody can prove otherwise]

# ---------------- The Tuscaran Glacier ----------------
@levels 35-50
the hrimthursa queen built her citadel over a dead dragon's bones. nobody asks what killed the dragon
king tuscar has a throne in the glacier too, but people only talk about queen kula. tells you who rules
our raid reached the mouth of tuscaran glacier once and turned back. the cold alone was enough
rumour says the jailer in tuscaran glacier holds one of the troll fathers. probably a story
the elder council of the hrimthursa sits right on the dragon's ribs. strange seat for a council
someday im climbing to the top of tuscaran glacier just to see what queen kula sees from up there

# ---------------- Aegir: Iarnvidiur, Modernagrav, the Valkyn ----------------
@levels 35-50
iarnvidiur breeds two-headed wolves [in the iarnwood|out in the iarnwood]. [two heads, twice the bite|twice the teeth], same bad temper
two of the wolves in iarnvidiur's lair are called hati and skoll. the old songs say they chase the sun and the moon
[i heard|heard] iarnvidiur is kin to the fenris [line|blood]. every bad wolf in midgard [goes back|leads back] to one den
the morvalt on modernagrav keep digging for something they call the mother. so far all they have is a skeleton the size of a longhouse
the crazed morvalt believe that when the mother wakes, trollheim wont be the only thing that falls
mortufoghus on modernagrav might be part of the mother, [some|people] [say|guess]. [i want|id want] proof
the valkyn were morvalt once, tamed by the troll fathers. then they came over to our side. i still watch them
a valkyn told me bodgar was here before odin came. i did not argue, he had the bigger axe
if you ask me, the morvalt dig because they lost something, not because they want something

# ---------------- Fenrir's Folly, Stungard, relics ----------------
@levels 10-50
silvertone in vasudheim tells [fenrir's folly|the tale of fenrir's folly] better after [three|a few] ales. [buy him one|bring coin]
i have heard silvertone tell the fenrir tale twice. never the same story twice
[the albs and hibs|they] call us stungard as if it were an insult. [we|i] call it [teamwork|winning]
first time i heard someone call midgard stungard i laughed. then i rolled a healer
thor's hammer and the horn of valhalla stay in midgard. anywhere else, they are on loan
[an old skald|my old guildmate] [swore|swears] there was a third relic, odin's [spear|eye], [lost|hidden] in the ice. no one has found it
the horn of valhalla blows when its carried off, some say. i have never heard it myself
old frontier vets get quiet when you ask what thor's hammer looked like on its stand

# ---------------- Crafters and drop myths ----------------
@who Crafter
@levels 20-50
[a smith|some crafter] told me dragon scale would make [armor|plate] [nobody|no one] can [pierce|crack]. never seen a scale myself
heard hrimthursa ice never melts. if you could forge it no blade would ever dull
the forgemaster in delling crater knows a recipe from before the gods, [so the dwarves say|they say]. [he wont share|he never shares]
[my tailor friend|an old tailor] swears the finest thread in midgard comes from spindelhalla. nobody [i know|ever] has [any to sell|some to sell]
[some say|i heard] a dverge in muspelheim can [work|fold] fire into a blade. [never met one who would talk|they never talk to me]

# ---------------- Levelers: is it worth it ----------------
@who Leveler
@levels 35-50
the drakulv camps in malmohus give decent xp, but every pull feels like the dragon is watching
i skip the iarnwood until 50. two-headed wolves are twice the biting for no extra xp
raumarik is good xp but the revenant walks there. watch your back
they tell new groups about the wretch of winter in raumarik to scare them. it worked on me

# ======================= Debates: Midgard lore =======================
# Second pass (2026-10-26): long scenes with the lore in the talk. Documented game lore is said plainly; the old Norse
# tales are "the old tale"; rumours and inventions are framed as belief, memory or a story someone told.
@kind debate
@realm mid

@topic lore_mid_odins_gate
@levels 5-50
@scene lore_mid_odins_gate
@role B type=Explorer
@role C type=NoLifer,Leveler levels=35-50
@role D type=* levels=5-25
@role E type=Socialite,Daredevil
A: {q} odin's gate has a giant, a glacier and no gate. anyone else think the road to asgard starts up there? | {q} a zone called odin's gate and not a door in sight. i keep wondering what it is the gate to
?D: wait, asgard like where the gods live? i thought odin's gate was just the frontier zone with the huge giant in it | asgard as in the gods' home? i only know odin's gate as the snowy frontier zone with the big giant
B: in the old tale asgard sits above midgard and the only road up is bifrost, a burning rainbow bridge. a bridge ends at a gate | the old tale is clear: you reach asgard over bifrost, the rainbow bridge, and someone keeps the far end. that is your gate
C: i've crossed odin's gate end to end on keep raids since the keeps were new. isalf, icestriders, wyverns, snow. no rainbow | ive run that zone more times than i can count. isalf camps, icestriders, a frore lich or two. if there's a bridge it hides well
B: look up instead of at your feet. the auroras up there are monsters, not weather. pale aurora, bright aurora. lights that walk and fight | that zone is full of auroras that fight back. pale ones, bright ones. lights with a con colour. what do you think bifrost left behind
?E: lights that walk over and hit you. some welcome from the gods | if thats the gods saying hello they need better manners
C: yggdra forest has a mob called northern light too, level thirty or so. glowing cold things live in cold zones, thats all it means | aurora mobs are wisps in a nicer colour. yggdra has killable northern lights as well and nobody calls yggdra a gate
B: then tell me why rainbow sprites live in jamtland. rainbow. in the snow, one zone from odin's gate, where nothing else has a colour | rainbow sprites, in jamtland, in the middle of a snowfield. the only colour in the north lives next door to odin's gate
D: ok but whats bifrost exactly. and who keeps the far end | sorry, who guards it? the bridge thing
B: heimdall, the gods' watchman. the old tale says he hears grass grow, sees a hundred leagues by night and sleeps less than a bird | heimdall, the white god. he hears the wool grow on a sheep, they say, and sees as well by night as by day. he watches the bridge
B: and he holds the gjallarhorn. when the end comes he blows it and every world hears. the horn is how asgard calls its army | he keeps a horn, the gjallarhorn. one blast and all nine worlds know ragnarok has begun
C: we have a horn. the horn of valhalla, in grallarhorn faste, and grallarhorn faste stands in yggdra forest. your gate is in the wrong zone | our horn relic sits in grallarhorn faste, which is in yggdra. if the horn is the key, the door is a zone away
B: listen to the name. grallarhorn, gjallarhorn. and the old tale says heimdall's horn lies hidden under the world tree. we keep it in yggdra | a temple named for heimdall's horn, in the forest named for the world tree, where the old tale says his horn was hidden. think
E: or the mason who cut the sign had a cold | or somebody misspelled it and nobody wanted to repaint
C: it's a relic. it makes our casters hit harder while it's home. i've walked it back to that temple myself and nothing in the sky opened | ive carried that horn home after the albs had it. the spells got stronger. no bridge came down
~ 15
A: fine, but somebody named the zone odin's gate for a reason | names come from somewhere though. who calls a snowfield a gate
C: the same folk who named every keep up there out of a skald's book. hlidskialf faste in jamtland is odin's high seat, and a jarl sits in it | same reason jamtland has hlidskialf faste, odin's high seat from the old tale. it holds a jarl, not a god
B: and look what they picked. hlidskialf to see all worlds from, fensalir for frigg's hall, arvakr for the horse that pulls the sun | thats my point. hlidskialf, odin's seat. fensalir, frigg's hall. arvakr, the sun's horse. our frontier is laid out like asgard
C: arvakr faste is in yggdra, fensalir in uppland, hlidskialf in jamtland. by that map asgard is the whole frontier and the hibs camp in it | they're spread over three zones. if that's asgard, the hibs have been sieging it every night for years
D: is the glacier giant guarding the gate then? he never moves off his spot | so the big giant is the guard? ive only ever seen him from far away
B: some say he's a frost giant older than the ice queen, set there to bar the way. in the old tale frost giants want asgard above all | a rime giant at asgard's door. the old tale says the frost giants always wanted in. who better to keep a door than the one who knocks
C: he throws anyone who gets close half a zone, i'll give you that. a guildie of mine landed by bledmeer faste and asked the guards for a rez | he throws people, sure. but a bouncer with no door behind him is just a big man standing in the snow
B: years back the heralds said fairies would pester him. who sends pests at a guard? someone who wants him looking the other way | there was word long ago that fairies were sent to bother the giant. ask yourself who wants the guard distracted
B: one more. the old tale gives heimdall nine mothers, all giantesses. gjalp, atla, jarnsaxa and six more. gjalp, as in gjalpinulva | and heimdall had nine giantess mothers in the old tale. one was gjalp. one was atla, like our fort. the giants and the gate go way back
~ 20
D: has anyone actually gone looking for a door up there | did anyone ever really look? like at night?
B: i have. behind the giant there's a ledge where the snow lies flat, like a step. after dark the auroras gather over it and never drift | i did. past the giant the snow on one ledge lies too flat. at night the lights hang over it and dont move
C: next keep raid through odin's gate you go stand on your step and say open. i'll watch from the hill | stand on it during the next raid and knock. if the sky opens i'll carry your bags to jordheim
E: and i'll take bets on where the giant throws you | i'll hold the pool. my coin says he lands you in uppland
A: i ride past bledmeer later anyway. i'll watch the lights | im up near bledmeer faste after this, ill look at the sky for you
B: count them. last time there were nine. heimdall had nine mothers | count the lights. i counted nine. you remember how many mothers heimdall had

@topic lore_mid_first_city
@levels 5-50
@scene lore_mid_first_city
@role B type=Explorer
@role C type=NoLifer levels=30-50
@role D type=* levels=5-25
@role E type=Crafter,Socialite
A: {q} if trollheim was the troll fathers' city, where did they live before it? nobody builds halls like that on the first try | {q} trollheim cant be the troll fathers' first city. it's too deep and too well made. so where was the first
D: who are the troll fathers? i play a troll and nobody ever told me | troll fathers? like trolls' grandparents? my race text never said
C: the old ones of aegir. they came before trolls and kobolds both, built trollheim, and tamed morvalt until the morvalt took it from them | precursors. trolls and kobolds both come down from them. their city is trollheim, out on aegir, and the morvalt overran it
B: and that's the point. the troll race text says they came out of the mountains to help us. mountains, not over the sea from an island | the race text says trolls came down out of the mountains to aid the norse. not across the water. so which of our mountains
C: gripklosa is all mountains and it's on aegir. done | gripklosa is nothing but mountains. trolls walked down from them. mystery solved
B: then why are there fallen trolls in jamtland and uppland? not morvalt, trolls, in our own frontier, a sea away from trollheim | explain the fallen trolls in jamtland then. dead trolls walking our frontier, nowhere near aegir. they came from somewhere close
?E: the fallen trolls are the ones who missed the boat home | maybe they just never found the ferry
C: jamtland also has undead vikings and ghoulish warriors. it's a graveyard of the frontier wars. a dead troll is not a map | they're frontier dead, like the undead vikings beside them. nobody says vikings had a secret city
B: think of the old tale. the sun turns trolls and dwarves to stone. thor kept the dwarf alviss talking all night and the dawn caught him | in the old stories daylight turns a troll to stone. thor kept the dwarf alviss answering riddles till sunrise, and that was the end of him
B: so the first city isn't under anything. it stands in the open, frozen. half the boulders in gripklosa are troll fathers caught by sunrise | the first city is out in plain sight. the big stones in the north are troll fathers who stayed up too late
E: my troll tank stands in the noon sun at the market all day. still not a rock. a bit red maybe | i group with a troll who stands in the sun every day. he complains, but he doesnt turn to stone
C: and we named a crater after delling, the dawn god of the old tale, and dellingstad sits in it full of folk who never turned to stone | delling crater is named for the dawn god, and people live in dellingstad just fine. so much for sunrise
B: or the dawn keeps the old things still. a crater named for sunrise, set where it can watch whatever sleeps in those hills | maybe thats why the crater sits where it does. the dawn guards the stones so they stay asleep
~ 15
D: so whats actually in trollheim? i only ever heard the name | is trollheim a dungeon? whats down there
C: a city gone bad. uppat and nedat gungledar, the up leader and the down leader. hem'varn guards. a trollkarl. and a bartender called olen | halls that go down forever. an up leader and a down leader, home guards, a trollkarl, and olen den bartender, who has never served a drink
E: i'd give a lot to know what olen brews. a recipe from the troll fathers would sell for a fortune | olen is a crafter's dream. imagine the recipes behind that bar
C: and at the bottom, nosdoden. if their first city still stood, the troll fathers wouldn't have dug their second over a beast like that | at the bottom sits nosdoden. nobody digs a second city over that thing if the first was still standing
B: unless the first fell to something worse. the hrimthursa sit on a dragon's bones in tuscaran. maybe they sit on a city as well | unless something took the first one. the ice queen built over bones in that glacier. bones and a city both, maybe
C: you just used the glacier to prove two theories in one night | ah, the glacier. where every midgard theory goes to sleep
E: there's that old story that the jailer up there keeps a troll father in a cell. somebody ask him for directions | the rumour goes that jailer vifil holds one of the troll fathers. ask the prisoner where he used to live
C: jailer vifil is in the eighties. ask him from a long way off | bring forty friends to that question
B: i'm in gripklosa this week. i'll look at the big stones at sunrise. if one has a face, everyone hears about it | next time im in gripklosa at dawn ill check the boulders for faces
A: if a rock waves back, send me a tell | if one of them waves, i want to know first

@topic lore_mid_dragon_gender
@levels 5-50
@scene lore_mid_dragon_gender
@role B class=Healer,Shaman,Skald
@role C type=NoLifer,Leveler levels=35-50
@role D type=* levels=5-25
@role E type=Socialite,Daredevil
A: {q} settle something for my guild. gjalpinulva, he or she? half of us say one, half the other | {q} raid chat fought for an hour over this: is our dragon a he or a she
C: every raid leader i ever followed into malmohus called the dragon he. he's turning, he's breathing, get out of his face | he. every raid i stood in, the leader said he. nobody argues grammar while on fire
B: the malmohus lore calls her a daughter of the fenris wolf. daughter. that's not a guess, it's what the old scouts wrote | the scouts' report on malmohus calls her fenris's daughter, plain as that
D: wait, whats the fenris wolf? | who is fenris? i keep hearing the name
B: the great wolf of the old tale, loki's son by a giantess. the gods feared him and bound him with a dwarf-made chain, gleipnir | loki's wolf son. he grew so big the gods were afraid, and they bound him with a chain the dwarves made from things that dont exist
B: tyr laid his hand in the wolf's jaws as a pledge it was only a game. when the chain held, the wolf bit it off | tyr put his hand in fenris's mouth to promise the chain was a test. it wasnt. thats why tyr has one hand
?E: one-handed god, and the warriors still swear by him | tyr, the only god who lost a hand keeping his word
C: so the dragon's father is a wolf. fine. a wolf can sire a he as easily as a she | ok, her father's a wolf. that tells you who the father is, not what the child is
B: then look at the name. gjalp was a giantess in the old tale, geirrod's daughter, who raised a river against thor. ulva sounds like she-wolf | the name itself. gjalp, the giantess thor drove off with a stone at the river. gjalpinulva, gjalp's she-wolf
C: you got she-wolf out of four letters. i get 'ouch' out of the whole word | thats a lot of meaning to squeeze out of ulva
B: and she bred the drakulvs. two legs, scales, wolf faces. scaled varg yearlings all over the ruins. who does the breeding in your raids? | the drakulvs are her brood, the scouts say she bred them. scaled vargs, young ones too. thats a mother's work
C: in the old tale loki turned mare and gave birth to sleipnir. there are sleipneirssons running round raumarik. birth proves nothing here | loki was a mare once and bore sleipnir. go look at the sleipneirssons in raumarik. midgard's gods dont follow your rules
?D: wait, loki had a horse? | hold on. loki was a horse's mother?
B: eight legs and all. odin rides him to this day, in the tale | an eight-legged one. odin's own horse. dont ask how
~ 15
E: from what i hear the hibs swear their glimmer king cuuldurach is the only male dragon. if theyre right, ours is a she | word is the hibs call cuuldurach the only male of the three. so ours is a she, if you trust hibs
C: the albs call golestandt she and the hibs call theirs he. that leaves us whatever we like | trust a hib on dragons. next they'll tell us the albs' stone dragon has a beard
B: she has drakulv disciples, missionaries, sacrificers, soultrappers. a whole priesthood. that's a mother goddess if i ever saw one | soultrappers keeping the souls of her dead, some say, and missionaries preaching for her. nobody builds a cult like that for a he
C: or a he with good priests | or a he who knows how to run a temple
E: the rumour is she talks to your corpse after she kills you. whoever goes next, listen for the voice | they say she speaks over your body after the breath. next raid, someone listen and tell us how it sounds
C: i always release before she gets a word in. i'm not lying in the dark waiting for a pronoun | i release too fast to hear anything. no pronoun is worth a corpse run in malmohus
B: the skalds sing she, the scouts wrote she. raid leaders yell he because they yell everything | the old songs say she, the lore says she. raid leaders call the rams he too
A: so she on paper and he in raid chat. sounds like midgard | she in the books, he on the field. my guild will love this
C: write it in the guild notes: whoever lives longest at the next raid gets to name it | next raid, whoever stays up longest decides. fair is fair

@topic lore_mid_giant_fire
@levels 15-50
@scene lore_mid_giant_fire
@role B type=NoLifer levels=40-50
@role C type=Leveler,Crafter levels=35-50
@role D type=* levels=15-30
@role E class=Runemaster,Spiritmaster,Healer,Shaman
A: {q} anyone still believe killing the glacier giant takes the fire out of the dragon? an old raid leader told me it like gospel | {q} heard it again: drop the glacier giant first and the dragon in malmohus breathes less. any truth in that
B: the story's as old as the dragon raids. in the first months a guild swore her breath was weak the week someone dropped the giant | i remember when it started. first winter of dragon raids. a guild said the breath went soft right after the giant fell, and it stuck
C: the giant stands in odin's gate, up in the frontier. malmohus is down in the old lands. what carries the fire across, a courier? | one is on the frontier and the other is at the far end of the realm. neither is in earshot of the other
D: why would a giant and a dragon even be connected? | sorry, why would they share anything? one is ice and the other is a wolf with wings
E: in the old tale the world began where the ice of niflheim met the fire of muspelheim in the great gap. the melt woke ymir | the old tale says it: ice from the north, fire from the south, and where they met in ginnungagap the first giant woke. one story
B: so the believers say the giant holds the cold and the dragon the heat. take one side away and the other has nothing to push against | a frost giant is the ice, the dragon's breath is the fire. kill one and the balance tips. thats the whole idea
C: then every isalf i kill in odin's gate weakens the fire giants in muspelheim. my xp is saving the realm | by that logic each ice lizard i kill helps the dverge with their forges. im a hero
?E: well, the fire giants in muspelheim are only level thirty. maybe someone has been killing isalf | the dverge do look tired lately
B: there's a second version too. kill the eldest drakulv first and she exhales less. half the raids i heard of tried that one | the other one goes: drop the oldest drakulv before the dragon and she breathes less often. that one at least is in the same ruins
C: that one i can almost believe. the old drakulv shouts for adds. fewer adds, fewer bodies standing in the cone when she breathes | the eldest calls for help. kill him first and fewer people are in front of her. thats tactics, not magic
B: and there was a reason it spread. one season her breath went soft overnight, and the giant had fallen that same week | i remember a stretch when one of her breaths hit lighter. whoever had dropped the giant that week took the credit
C: that was the change that softened one breath on every dragon at once. the hibs and albs noticed it too, and they have no glacier giant | the heralds turned down one of each dragon's breaths. the albs' dragon got it too. golestandt has no giant
~ 20
E: whatever you believe, rule one never changed: nobody nukes until the tanks hold her. that does more than any giant | i'll say this. every breath i saw wipe a raid started with an eager caster, not a giant
D: so does anyone know for sure? did anyone count the breaths? | has anybody actually counted, both ways?
B: nobody counts anything in a dragon raid. you count heals and you pray | counting while youre on fire is harder than it sounds
C: then it stays a superstition, like tapping your shield before trollheim. harmless, but dont plan a raid around it | it's a story, same as not saying her name inside the ruins
E: i say her name in malmohus all the time. i also die a lot in there | i've said her name in the ruins. i won't tell you how that night ended
C: and half the raid goes for the luminescent stones anyway. fifty respec stones. nobody marches to odin's gate first for that | most of the raid is there for the respec stones. nobody would cross the realm for the giant's teeth
B: next time the realm forms up for her i'll keep a tally. breaths per minute, giant up or down. then we'll know | i'll count at the next raid, with a notepad, and ask whether the giant is up. somebody has to
A: i'll hold your notes if the breath gets you first | ill take the tally if you go down

@topic lore_mid_ragnarok
@levels 5-50
@scene lore_mid_ragnarok
@role B type=NoLifer,Socialite levels=30-50
@role C type=Leveler,Explorer
@role D type=* levels=5-25
@role E class=Spiritmaster,Runemaster,Shaman,Bonedancer
A: {q} serious one. has ragnarok already happened and we just live in the after? the more i look the more i think so | {q} anyone else think we missed ragnarok? giants everywhere, gods quiet, wolves in every cave
D: what is ragnarok exactly? people say it like i should know | ragnarok? i hear it in jordheim but nobody explains
E: the doom of the gods in the old tale. fenrir breaks his chain and swallows odin, thor and the serpent kill each other, surt burns the world | the end of the gods. the wolf gets loose and eats odin, thor kills the midgard serpent and dies of its poison, fire giants burn it all
E: and before it comes the fimbulwinter. three winters back to back, no summer between, and brothers kill brothers | first comes fimbulwinter. three winters with no summer, war everywhere. then the wolves catch the sun and moon
B: three winters. look at our frontier: uppland, yggdra, jamtland, odin's gate. snow in every one, and the realm war all around it | four zones of snow and the realms at war in them every night. that is the fimbulwinter, right there
C: midgard was cold before any of us made a character. snow is not a prophecy | the north has snow. thats not the end of the world, thats weather
B: then why do the names fit? vindsaul faste is named for vindsval, father of winter in the old tale. svasud faste for svasud, summer's father | vindsaul and svasud. in the old tale those are the fathers of winter and summer. both have a faste on our road
C: and summer's faste is the one holding the border gate, guards and all. you just proved summer is still standing | svasud faste still stands at the frontier with guards in it. sounds like summer is holding fine
B: the wolves then. skoll chases the sun, hati the moon, and at ragnarok they catch them. so where are skoll and hati now? | in the old tale two wolves chase the sun and moon until the end. skoll and hati. tell me where those two live these days
C: in iarnvidiur's lair on aegir, both of them, sitting in a cave. if they were done with the sun they'd look happier | iarnvidiur's lair, level sixty nine each. which means theyre not up in the sky chasing anything
B: or they caught it already and came home to sleep it off. look how dark it gets in the iarnwood | maybe they ate and went home. the iarnwood is dark enough for it
E: their cave belongs to a giantess who breeds wolves. the old tale has that too: a giantess in jarnvidr, the iron wood, bearing the sun-wolves | iarnvidiur, the woman of the iarnwood. in the old tale an old giantess of the iron wood bears the wolf brood, skoll and hati among them
?D: so the iarnwood is the iron wood from the story? | wait, its the same story?
E: the story came first. the iarnwood just kept its old name | the name is older than any of us. it carried over
~ 15
C: here's my problem. fenrir has to break loose first. the scouts call gjalpinulva his daughter, not his widow. he's still bound somewhere | the wolf breaking free is how ragnarok starts. his daughter sits in malmohus waiting. so he's still chained
B: raumarik has fenrir soldiers, mystics and a greater fenrir. jamtland has fenrir prophets out in the snow. prophets of what, if not the end? | fenrir prophets in jamtland, fenrir mystics in raumarik. somebody out there is announcing something
C: raumarik also has a wolf of loki and a pack of winter wolves. it's a kennel, not a prophecy | a cold zone with wolves in it has wolf names. that's all
E: the fire giants worry me more. surt leads them over bifrost at the end. ours in muspelheim are guards, lookouts and scouts. scouts for what? | at the end surt's fire giants ride over the bridge. the ones in muspelheim are lookouts and watchmen. somebody is watching for something
C: they're level thirty. if that's the host of muspel, ragnarok is a lowbie camp | thirty, the lot of them. if thats surt's army i'll hold the bridge myself with a training sword
B: or the shade of gunnar walks muspelheim because the heroes already fell there. ghosts stay where somebody lost | the shade of gunnar is down there too. heroes leave ghosts where they died. maybe the fight already happened
E: the old tale says naglfar, the ship of the dead, is built from dead men's uncut nails. keep yours trimmed and it takes longer to finish | hel's ship naglfar is made of the nails of the dead, in the old tale. cut yours short and you slow the end down
?D: is that why my healer cuts his nails before raids? | wait, people actually do that?
B: half the old raiders i knew did. call it insurance | some of the old guard swear by it. cheap superstition
C: so it's over or it hasn't started, and either way i still have to pay for my armour | its over or its coming, and my armour still needs farming
A: i'll vote hasn't started. the realm still has work for us | not yet, please. i've got plans for this realm
B: trim your nails tonight then. just in case | either way, cut your nails. it costs nothing

@topic lore_mid_valkyn_trust
@levels 5-50
@scene lore_mid_valkyn_trust
@role B type=NoLifer,Leveler levels=30-50
@role C class=Bonedancer
@role D type=* levels=5-25
@role E type=Explorer,Socialite
A: {q} be honest, do you all trust the valkyn? they turned on the troll fathers once. what stops them turning on us | {q} question nobody likes: the valkyn guard our towns on aegir. should they?
D: who are the valkyn? i saw guards in bjarken with that name | i only know valkyn as the guards in bjarken. whats their story
B: they were morvalt, the savages of aegir. the troll fathers tamed some, and those broke the leash and came over to us | morvalt, tamed by the troll fathers and made into soldiers. they rebelled against their masters and sided with midgard
B: and you've seen the rest of the morvalt. spear, axe and sword masters in trollheim, crazed schamen in faraheim. that's the stock | the untamed ones still fill trollheim, spjut masters and yxa masters and crazed shamans. thats where the valkyn come from
C: they broke a leash put on them by masters who chained them. thats not betrayal, its getting up off your knees | they left owners, not friends. any of us would have done the same
B: and they pray to bodgar, a god of the dead older than odin, they say. nobody in jordheim lights a candle for him | their god is bodgar, a death god from before odin came. not our gods, not our houses
C: i pray to bodgar. the house of bodgar trains every bonedancer in this realm. say that again slower | careful. bodgar's house taught me every spell i cast. if he's a reason to doubt them, doubt me too
?E: ha, he has you there | the bonedancer wins that round
B: you came up through a house in jordheim. the valkyn came up under troll fathers' whips. not the same road | your house sits in jordheim among our gods. theirs sat in trollheim under someone else's
E: the old tale has this exact thing. the aesir and vanir fought, then swapped hostages. njord and freyr came to asgard and became gods there | in the old tale the gods warred with the vanir and ended it with hostages. freyr and freyja ended up gods of asgard
E: enemies one year, family the next, and nobody calls freyr a traitor. freyja even shares the slain with odin | old enemies got the best seats in asgard. freyja takes half the fallen, odin the other half
B: the gods also took in loki and made him odin's blood brother. ask balder how that went | loki was adopted too. blood brother to odin. balder ended up dead because of it
?D: who is balder? | wait, whats with balder?
E: odin's brightest son. everything in the world swore not to harm him except the mistletoe. loki found it | the shining god. every thing swore never to hurt him, except a sprig of mistletoe. loki put it in a blind god's hand
~ 15
C: i've watched valkyn guards in gripklosa and munin sound die at their posts against morvalt raiders. never seen one leave a gate open | valkyn guards hold the line on aegir. they die where they're posted. more than some players do
B: for now. the morvalt still dig on modernagrav for the mother. the day she wakes, ask which side the valkyn stand on | the morvalt want the mother woken. when that happens we'll see whose side bodgar picks
C: bodgar is a god of the dead. if the mother is a corpse, he'd want her to stay one | a death god wants the dead kept dead. the valkyn would be first to bury her again
E: the way i heard it, when trollheim fell the valkyn didn't stay to loot it. they walked across to us instead | a skald told me they could have kept trollheim for themselves and chose to come to midgard. if that's true it counts
B: or they went where the winning side was | or they saw who was winning and picked
A: so trust them, but sleep with your back to a wall | trust them and keep an eye open. sounds like every alliance ive been in
C: come by bjarken some time. the valkyn at the gate nod at bonedancers. stand next to me and maybe they'll nod at you | the guards in bjarken know me. walk in with me and see how they treat a friend

@topic lore_mid_mother
@levels 5-50
@scene lore_mid_mother
@role B type=Explorer
@role C type=Leveler,NoLifer levels=40-50
@role D type=* levels=5-25
@role E class=Shaman,Healer,Skald
A: {q} what do you think the morvalt are really digging up on modernagrav? they call it the mother | {q} the mother on modernagrav. old bones, or something thats going to wake up
D: modernagrav? i've never heard of it | is modernagrav on aegir? i only know aegir's landing
C: the little island off aegir that turned up not long ago. long forgotten, the heralds said. full of morvalt with shovels | one of the forgotten islands that were found not long ago, off the shore of aegir. the morvalt got there first and started digging
B: they dig round a skeleton half buried in the hill, ribs as long as a longhouse. they call it the mother and talk about the day she wakes | a giant's bones lie half sunk in the ground there and the morvalt work around them day and night. the mother, they call her
E: in the old tale the first giant was ymir. odin and his brothers killed him and made the world from him. his bones are the hills | the old tale starts with ymir. odin cut him up and built the world. flesh to soil, bones to mountains, skull to sky
B: so maybe the mother is a piece of ymir the gods missed. the shamans hint at it, and they serve the house of ymir | the house of ymir trains our shamans. ask one about the mother and watch him go quiet
?E: i'll neither confirm nor deny | some things the gothi of ymir doesnt say out loud
C: or it's a mammoth. the island is full of decaying mammoths walking about. look at what's actually there | the island crawls with decaying mammoths. big bones on an island of big dead animals. not a mystery
B: a mammoth is the size of a cart. those ribs arch over your head like rafters. no mammoth ever lay down that big | i've stood under those ribs. they go over you like a hall roof. no mammoth i ever skinned was that long
D: why call it the mother though? i thought giants were men | why a mother, if its a giant?
E: ymir had a mother of sorts. audhumla, the great cow, who fed him her milk and licked the first god out of the salt ice | in the tale ymir drank from audhumla, the first cow. she licked the ice until the first god came out. a mother to everyone
?D: the world started with a cow? | we have a cow goddess?
E: a very large cow. show some respect | the biggest cow there ever was. and yes, we owe her
C: so the morvalt are digging up a cow. someone tell mortufoghus his life's work is a cowshed | i love this. the scariest thing on that island is guarding a cow
B: then why does mortufoghus guard the dig? he's in the seventies. nobody posts a guard like that over a cowshed | bones don't need a guard of seventy seven. mortufoghus stands over that dig like it matters to someone
C: the morvalt post guards over everything. there are morvalt vaktare on that island watching plain dirt | morvalt put watchmen on their latrines. a big guard proves they're morvalt, nothing else
~ 20
B: and they have morvalt gravmaniska, grave maniacs in their own tongue, and reanimated howlers walking again. something there raises the dead | grave-digger morvalt with a madness name, and dead howlers back on their feet. something on that island wakes dead things already
E: the crazed ones say when the mother wakes, trollheim won't be the only thing that falls. that's their prayer, not ours | the morvalt say trollheim falls when she wakes. they say it smiling
C: they said trollheim would fall, and it did, to them. their prophecies are just their plans said slowly | the morvalt already took trollheim once. when a morvalt prophesies, he's telling you his plans
A: so a giant, a cow or a mammoth. lovely choice | bones of a god or of a cow. great
B: i'm going out to modernagrav this week to pace the ribs. more than a longhouse and you owe me an ale | i'll walk those ribs end to end myself. if they're longer than a longhouse, the ale is on you
C: and if it moos, run. and i get your horse | if anything moos at you, leave. and i want your horse

@topic lore_mid_oldest
@levels 5-50
@scene lore_mid_oldest
@role B type=Crafter,Leveler
@role C class=Shaman,Bonedancer,Runemaster
@role D type=Explorer
@role E type=* levels=5-25
A: {q} what's the oldest thing in midgard? not the oldest player, the oldest thing | {q} tavern argument: who or what was in midgard first
B: the dwarves. oldest race, devoted to the elder gods. it's in the race text and every dwarf will read it to you | dwarves. the race text says it outright: oldest race in midgard, devoted to the elder gods
C: older than the dwarves are the giants. ymir was first of all, before gods and men | the giants were here before the dwarves. ymir came before anything that has a name
B: any dwarf will tell you they were digging before the gods learned to talk | ask a dwarf. they were mining before the giants had names
C: the old tale says the dwarves woke as maggots in ymir's dead flesh, and the gods gave them wits. sorry | in the old tale the dwarves began as maggots in ymir's body. the gods gave them minds later
?E: maggots? | wait, dwarves were maggots?
B: that's a giant's story. dwarves forged mjolnir and gungnir. show me a maggot that can work a forge | slander. dwarves made thor's hammer and odin's spear. no maggot ever swung a smith's hammer
?D: i would not say maggot anywhere near delling crater | forgemaster brungar would like a word about that maggot thing
C: then bodgar. the valkyn swear their god of the dead was here before odin came | bodgar. the valkyn say their death god was old when odin's people arrived
B: every god is older than odin to the folk who pray to it | the valkyn say a lot to make their god sound important
D: i'll go with the troll fathers. they came before trolls and kobolds both, and trollheim is older than any hall in jordheim | the troll fathers. they made trollheim and came before two whole races. they must have been old when the dwarves were young
?E: who are the troll fathers? | the troll fathers are real? i thought that was a joke about old trolls
D: the old people of aegir. trolls and kobolds both come down from them. the morvalt sit in their halls now | the first people of the isle. trolls and kobolds descend from them. now morvalt live in their city
~ 15
C: look at the names. muspelheim has a seer of ancient dawning. iarnvidiur's lair an ancient syver. tuscaran has something called fornfrusenen | the names say a lot. a seer of ancient dawning in muspelheim. fornfrusenen in the glacier, frozen long ago, near enough
D: fornfrusenen is the one i'd bet on. something frozen in that glacier since before the queen came | frozen long ago, in a glacier built on a dragon. that is old
B: older still is the dragon under the glacier. the queen built on its bones, so it was dead and old before she came | the dragon the citadel stands on was dead before the hrimthursa arrived. dead and already old
C: the norns are older than all of it. they sat at the well under yggdrasil spinning fate before the first giant opened his eyes | the three norns at the well under the world tree. they spun the threads for everything in this argument
E: is the world tree real? i've been to yggdra forest and it's just snow and frost giants | wait, yggdra forest has the tree? i only saw frost giants and wolves there
D: nobody's found it. could be the hills up there are its roots and we walk on them | not that anyone's seen. i think the ridges might be roots
B: so the oldest thing in midgard is a tree nobody's found, kept by three women nobody's met | so your answer is a tree that isnt there
D: the oldest thing is always the one nobody's found yet. that's how you know it's old | the oldest one is the one still hidden. thats the point
A: good answer. now i want to go digging | i like that. i'm going looking
B: take a dwarf. they know how to dig, and not as maggots | bring a dwarf along. the digging part they have down

@topic lore_mid_glacier_bones
@levels 5-50
@scene lore_mid_glacier_bones
@role B type=NoLifer levels=40-50
@role C type=Explorer
@role D type=* levels=5-25
@role E type=Crafter,Daredevil
A: {q} whose bones did the ice queen build her citadel on? somebody killed a dragon up there before the hrimthursa came | {q} the citadel in tuscaran sits on a dragon's bones. which dragon? nobody ever says
D: what citadel? whats tuscaran? | tuscaran glacier? i only know the name
B: the ice dungeon on aegir. the hrimthursa frost giants rule it: queen kula, king tuscar, an elder council and their icelords | the glacier dungeon on the isle. hrimthursa frost giants, queen kula on top, king tuscar beside her, a council of elders, icelords
B: and the whole citadel is raised over a dead dragon's bones. the elder council sits right on the ribs | their citadel stands on a dragon's skeleton. the council chairs sit right on its ribs
C: i say it's gjalpinulva's mother. the old wolf dragon dies in the ice, the daughter flies south and nests in malmohus | gjalpinulva's mother, if you ask me. the old dragon died up north and the daughter moved down to malmohus
B: the scouts say gjalpinulva's father is the fenris wolf. why would her mother be a dragon too? | the dragon's father is a wolf, the lore says. a dragon mother makes no sense
C: then fenris had a dragon for a mate. the scales on the drakulvs came from somewhere | then fenris married a dragon. explains the scales
?E: midgard family trees are a mess | every family in the old tales is like this
C: or nosdoden's kin. trollheim and the glacier are both on aegir, and they say nosdoden was a true dragon before he was changed | nosdoden was a proper dragon once, they say, before trollheim twisted him. same island, same family maybe
B: nosdoden leaves an apparition for every adventurer he kills. whatever he is now, he's not anyone's kin | nosdoden makes copies of the dead. thats not a dragon, thats a curse with teeth
~ 15
C: the old tale has a better candidate. nidhogg, the dragon that gnaws the root of the world tree in the cold below | in the old tale a dragon called nidhogg chews at yggdrasil's root down in the cold. if any dragon lies dead in ice, its him
B: nidhogg isn't dead in the tale. he flies up at the very end carrying corpses on his wings | in the tale nidhogg outlives ragnarok. he's the last thing you see, flying over the field with the dead
C: so if he's dead in tuscaran, the end came and he lost. which some here already believe | if those bones are nidhogg's, ragnarok is behind us. see, it fits
E: crafter's question: has anyone looked at those bones up close? the hrimthursa have sculptors and icesplitters in there | the hrimthursa keep sculptors. maybe the dragon is ice carved to look like bones, for show
B: i've fought the sculptors. they shape ice walls. nobody carves a whole dragon to sit on | hrimthursa sculptors, yes, they carve ice. nobody carves a skeleton that size for decoration
E: you'd be surprised what a queen will sit on | kings sit on stranger thrones than that
D: who could kill a dragon that big anyway? | so who killed it, if its real?
B: the hrimthursa are the rime giants of the old tale, children of bergelmir, the one giant who lived through the flood of ymir's blood | in the old tale the frost giants come from bergelmir, who rode out the flood when ymir died. old enough to have seen it fall
C: and there's a hrimthursa berg in there. maybe named for the old one | they have a mob called hrimthursa berg. could be family
E: i still say the jailer has something worse than prisoners down there. someone had to lock the dragon in | or jailer vifil did it. he has a whole prison, someone had to put the dragon in it
A: no answer, but a good story for a cold night | nobody knows, and i bet the queen likes it that way
C: one day i'll reach the council chamber and knock on a rib. bone sounds different from ice | i want to stand on those ribs and knock. if it rings hollow it's ice, dull and it's bone
B: bring a raid. the elders hit hard | bring forty friends. the council doesnt like visitors

@topic lore_mid_relic_third
@levels 5-50
@scene lore_mid_relic_third
@role B type=NoLifer,Socialite levels=35-50
@role C type=Crafter,Leveler
@role D type=Daredevil,Explorer
@role E type=* levels=5-25
A: {q} was there ever a third midgard relic? the old skalds sing about one besides the hammer and the horn | {q} two relics, thor's hammer and the horn of valhalla. anyone else think there should be a third
E: what do the relics even do? i just see people running them around | sorry, whats a relic for? i see the raids but never understood
B: while they sit in their temples, thor's hammer makes our fighters hit harder and the horn our spells. lose one and everyone feels it | the hammer strengthens our melee, the horn our casters. as long as they're home in mjollner faste and grallarhorn faste
B: and an old skald sang me of a third, odin's spear gungnir, lost in the ice when the giants came south. never found | the skalds have a third one, gungnir, odin's spear. lost when the frost came down, the old songs say
C: two relics, two temples, same as the albs and the hibs. if there were a seventh, someone would have a spare temple | every realm has two. mjollner faste in uppland, grallarhorn faste in yggdra. no empty pedestal anywhere
B: when relics first came, the heralds said more would follow. i remember it. years on, still six. so where did the plan go? | the heralds promised more relics when the first six appeared. they never came. something was meant to be added
C: plans change. that proves somebody planned, not that a spear is lying in the snow | a promise isnt a spear
D: in the old tale loki bet his head against two dwarves, and they forged three treasures: mjolnir, the ring draupnir and the boar gullinbursti | the old tale has loki betting his head with two dwarf smiths. they made the hammer, a gold ring and a golden boar. three gifts
D: and before that the sons of ivaldi made three more: gungnir, the ship skidbladnir and sif's gold hair. the gods' treasures come in threes | before that came the spear, the folding ship and sif's golden hair. treasures in threes, twice over
?E: the gods have a ship that folds up? | wait, a ship you fold into your pocket?
C: skidbladnir, freyr's. folds like cloth, they say. i'd trade every recipe i know for that one | freyr keeps it in a pouch. as a crafter i want that pattern more than any relic
C: but your threes fall apart. the horn is heimdall's, not a dwarf gift. the hammer is the only one of those treasures we hold | the horn of valhalla was never a dwarf's work. so we have one of the dwarves' treasures, not two of three
B: then the third is the one that answers the horn. heimdall blows it, odin rides out with gungnir. horn calls, hammer strikes, spear leads | horn, hammer, spear. the horn calls the gods, thor answers, odin leads. the skalds always sang it as three
~ 15
C: if odin's spear were lying in midgard, the forgemaster in delling crater would have sold it by now | brungar in delling crater would have melted it down for nails. lets be honest
D: or the dwarves of delling know and won't say. they never tell you anything | ask the delling dwarves and they smile and change the subject. that's not ignorance
B: and here's the part nobody likes. find a third and the albs and hibs come for it the next night | three relics means three temples to lose. every alb and hib in the frontier would know by morning
?D: better a temple to lose than a spear in the snow | id rather lose it in a fight than leave it in the ice
C: hold the two we have first. half the realm can't keep track of those | we lose sight of two often enough already
D: i'm swimming along the ice edge this week anyway. if something shines under the water, i'm diving | im going swimming north past the coast soon. if a spear sticks up out of the ice, its mine
E: can i come? i don't know what a spear looks like under ice but i want to see | can i tag along? i swim fast and i want to see the edge of the ice
B: if you find it, send me a tell before anyone else. i want to carry it to the temple | bring a healer, and tell me first. i want to be the one who carries it home

# ---------------- Tales: one bot tells a legend, the others cut in ----------------

@topic lore_tale_werewolves_malmohus
@levels 5-50
@scene mid_tale_werewolves_malmohus
@role B type=NoLifer,Explorer levels=30-50
@role C type=* levels=5-25
@role D type=Socialite,Daredevil
A: {q} ever wondered why the werewolves of skona won't set foot in malmohus? an old ranger told me the story once | {q} here's a story for you: why skona's werewolves stay clear of malmohus
B: the scouts wrote the first part plainly: werewolves avoid the place and the svartalfar spy on it from the edges. the why is the old part | the malmohus report says the werewolves won't go in. what it doesn't say is why
C: werewolves? like the ones in skona ravine? | skona has werewolves? i've only been to the edge of it
B: a whole people of them. captains, warders, couriers, a werewolf shaman. their king hresvelgr sits in varulvhamn | a nation of them. lieutenants, guards, a shaman. and king hresvelgr in varulvhamn rules them all
A: the way i heard it, they were wolf-coat warriors once, men who wore the pelt into battle until the pelt wore them | so the story goes, they were men who put on the wolf skin for battle and one day couldnt take it off
A: they kept one law: a wolf answers to the pack, never a master. then a dragon, half wolf, settled in malmohus and bred wolves to serve her | their one rule was that a wolf has no master. then the wolf-headed dragon came to malmohus and started making wolves of her own
A: two legs, scales, wolf faces. drakulvs. wolves that kneel. the ranger said every werewolf knows that's what he'd become if she caught him | drakulvs. wolves bred to kneel to a dragon. to a werewolf, he said, thats worse than death, and its what waits for them inside
B: that she bred the drakulvs is in the scouts' report. the kneeling part is what the old rangers said. i believe one and a half of it | the breeding is fact. the fear of turning into one is the tale. i half believe the tale
D: or they've just seen the breath. smart wolves | or they know about the breath. no tale needed
A: there's more. any werewolf who strays in comes out with scales on his paws, and his own pack runs him out of skona before the full moon | and the ranger swore a werewolf who goes in grows scales on his hands, and the pack drives him off
B: it would explain the scaled vargs in there. wolves with scales, yearlings too. i always wondered where she got the stock | that fits the scaled varg yearlings all over the ruins, i'll give him that
~ 15
A: and that's why the svartalfar watch from the edges, he said. they're waiting to see if the werewolves ever go in to take back their own | the svartalfar sit at the edge waiting for the day the werewolves come to fetch their lost
C: i'll never look at a drakulv the same way | thats grim. i almost feel sorry for the drakulvs now
D: feel sorry all you like, they still drop coin | i'll still kill them. pity doesnt pay for armour

@topic lore_tale_fenris_daughter
@levels 5-50
@scene mid_tale_fenris_daughter
@role B type=* levels=5-25
@role C type=NoLifer,Leveler levels=35-50
@role D type=Socialite,Crafter
A: {q} want the tale of how the fenris wolf got a daughter with wings? my grandmother told it every winter | {q} gather round, i'll tell the one about the wolf's daughter in malmohus
B: the dragon has a story? i thought she was just a raid boss | the dragon? isnt she just a dragon?
A: first the father. fenris grew till only tyr dared feed him. the gods made two chains, leyding and dromi, and he snapped both | first the father. only tyr was brave enough to feed fenris. the gods made two chains for him, and the wolf broke them like straw
A: so the dwarves made gleipnir from a cat's footstep, a woman's beard, a mountain's roots, a bear's sinews, a fish's breath and a bird's spit | the third chain was dwarf work: footfall of a cat, beard of a woman, roots of a mountain, breath of a fish, spit of a bird
A: and it held. tyr lost his hand. the wolf lay bound on an island, and the slaver from his jaws ran out into a river | it held, tyr lost his hand, and the wolf lay chained with his jaws propped open, drooling a whole river
A: here my gran went past the old tale. a giantess of the iron wood came to the bound wolf by night, and the pup she bore grew scales and wings | then gran's part: a giantess came to the chained wolf in the dark, and her pup was born with scales from the cold of the chain
C: that's your gran's bit. no skald i know sings it | thats not in any saga i've heard. sounds like a winter's night invention
A: maybe. but the scouts who mapped malmohus call her fenris's daughter, and the scouts never met my gran | could be. still, the malmohus report calls her his daughter. gran didnt write that
A: and the mother, gran said, was iarnvidiur, who breeds two-headed wolves in the iarnwood. so skoll and hati are the dragon's brothers | the mother was the giantess who breeds wolves in the iarnwood, gran said. so the dragon has kin on aegir
C: two-headed wolves on aegir and a wolf-headed dragon in malmohus. i'll grant you the family look | iarnvidiur's wolves and gjalpinulva do look related, i'll give gran that
~ 15
A: the last part: she bred the drakulvs to be the pack her father never had. when there are enough, they march north to gnaw his chain | and the end: she raises the drakulvs as her father's army. one day they go looking for wherever he's bound
D: there are drakulv missionaries and disciples in there. a pack doesn't need missionaries. an army does | they have missionaries. who sends missionaries unless they want converts
B: so every drakulv killed keeps the wolf chained a little longer? | wait, so killing drakulvs keeps fenris bound?
A: that's how gran told it. it's why she sent every one of us to malmohus once we were old enough | thats what gran said, and she was never wrong about wolves

@topic lore_tale_troll_fathers
@levels 5-50
@scene mid_tale_troll_fathers
@role B type=* levels=5-25
@role C type=NoLifer levels=35-50
@role D class=Bonedancer,Warrior,Shaman,Thane
A: {q} want the tale of the troll fathers and the morvalt? it's why aegir looks the way it does | {q} let me tell you how trollheim fell. a troll in bjarken told it to me over too many ales
B: troll fathers? are they real trolls? | real trolls, or old stories?
A: real enough. the old ones of aegir, before trolls and kobolds. both peoples come down from them. they dug trollheim deep into the rock | the first people of aegir. trolls and kobolds both descend from them, and they built trollheim down into the island
C: that much is the known part. after that, everyone tells it a different way | the first bit is solid. past that every troll has his own version
A: the morvalt were the wild ones of the isle. the troll fathers caught some, tamed them and set them on their gates. those became the valkyn | there were savages on the island, the morvalt. the troll fathers broke some to the halter and made them guards. the valkyn
A: the troll i heard it from said the fathers grew lazy. too many servants, too few eyes. they gave the valkyn every key and went below | the way he told it, the fathers stopped watching. the valkyn held every door while the old ones slept below
A: then the valkyn turned, every telling agrees. but my troll swore they never let the morvalt in. they walked out and left the doors open | the valkyn rebelled, sure. but he said they didnt open the gates to the morvalt. they left, and the gates stood open after them
C: that's a troll being kind. a morvalt schamen would tell you it was the plan all along | a kind telling. ask a crazed morvalt and it was all his idea
A: either way the wild morvalt came through open doors and took the city. the fathers went deeper, and some say they still live below nosdoden | whatever the cause, the morvalt poured in. the fathers fled down, and some say they're still under nosdoden's hall
?B: who's nosdoden? | is nosdoden a boss?
C: a dragon gone wrong at the bottom of trollheim. every adventurer he kills leaves an apparition of him until they're rezzed | a twisted dragon in the deepest hall. kill a man and an apparition of nosdoden stays until someone rezzes him
~ 15
D: and the valkyn came to us, swore by bodgar and guard our towns on aegir now. same job they had for the fathers, new masters | funny how it ends. the valkyn stand at gates again, ours this time
A: that's the bit the troll liked least. he poured his ale on the floor, said 'gates', and walked out | when he got to that part the troll tipped his ale out on the boards and never finished the sentence
B: now i want to see trollheim. from very far away | i want to see those gates someday. from a safe hill

@topic lore_tale_ice_queen
@levels 5-50
@scene mid_tale_ice_queen
@role B type=* levels=5-25
@role C type=Explorer
@role D type=NoLifer,Daredevil levels=40-50
A: {q} here's the tale of how queen kula raised her citadel on a dragon's bones. a skald in jordheim sings it if you pay him | {q} i'll tell the ice queen's story the way a skald sang it to me
B: ice queen? is she the boss of tuscaran? | whose queen? the frost giants'?
A: she rules the hrimthursa, the rime giants of the glacier. in the old tale they come from bergelmir, who outlived the flood when ymir died | the hrimthursa are the rime giants, children of bergelmir, who rode out the flood of ymir's blood when the gods killed him
A: the skald says kula was the coldest of bergelmir's line. her brothers marched south for green land. she stayed and wanted winter for good | in his song kula was the youngest and coldest. the others wanted the green lands. she wanted the north forever
D: she got her wish. the cold in there bites harder than the icelords | well, she got it. i've been up there. you can lose your fingers just looking at the walls
A: she found a dragon dead in the ice, ribs wide as a fjord, and said here i'll build, on a thing so big no summer can melt it | she came on a dragon frozen in the glacier and built on top of it, because nothing that big ever thaws
C: the citadel on the bones is real, every guide says so. the coldest daughter part is the skald's | that she built over bones is the true part. i've never heard the daughter bit anywhere else
A: then she took king tuscar for husband, but the throne was always hers. the elder council sit on the ribs because she lets them | king tuscar came later, the skald says, and never ruled. the elders on the ribs sit there by her grace
D: true enough. the glacier carries tuscar's name and every raid only talks about kula | i've noticed that. nobody talks about tuscar, and his name's on the door
~ 15
A: her royal iceweaver mends the walls each night so they never crack, and jailer vifil keeps a cell for every enemy she ever named | her iceweavers weave the walls new every night. and the jailer holds a cell for each enemy she has
C: the rumour is one cell holds a troll father. i went as deep as i dared and never got near it | they say one of those cells has a troll father in it. never got close enough to look
B: why keep them all alive? | why keep prisoners at all?
A: for fimbulwinter. when the three winters come she opens the cells and takes every prisoner south in chains | the skald says she waits for the fimbulwinter. when the long winter comes, the cells open and she marches south with them
C: he says the dragon's skull sits behind her throne. i want to see that before i quit | one day i'll reach the throne room and see if the skull is really behind her chair

@topic lore_tale_fenrirs_folly
@levels 5-50
@scene mid_tale_fenrirs_folly
@role B type=Socialite levels=20-50
@role C type=* levels=5-25
@role D type=NoLifer,Leveler levels=30-50
A: {q} anyone heard silvertone in vasudheim tell fenrir's folly? i got him going not long ago and remember most of it | {q} silvertone told me fenrir's folly again. here's how it went, near as i remember
C: who's silvertone? | silvertone? is that a merchant?
B: an old fellow in vasudheim with a tale for every ale. fenrir's folly is his big one | a storyteller in vasudheim. buy him a drink and you get the tale whether you want it or not
A: he starts with himself young and greedy, hunting far north, following a wolf track as wide as a cart | the way he tells it he was young and stupid, chasing a wolf track as big as a cart across the snow
D: it gets bigger every time. when i heard it the track was big enough to stable horses in | in my version the track was the size of a longhouse. it grows with the ale
A: at the end of the track the snow is torn up, and in it lies a ribbon, soft as silk, running off toward the sea | he finds where the track ends, and in the snow there's a ribbon thin as silk going off over the ice
B: that's gleipnir. in the old tale the chain that binds fenris looks like a silk ribbon. the old liar knows his sagas | ha, the ribbon. gleipnir looked like silk in the old tale too. he's clever, silvertone
A: so of course he coils it up to sell in jordheim, follows it, and at the far end something breathes like a forge | he winds it up thinking it'll fetch a good price, and at the other end he hears breathing like a smithy bellows
C: please tell me he didn't pull it | he didnt tug it, did he?
A: he did. hence the folly. a yellow eye opens in the snow, big as a door, and he drops the ribbon and runs till his boots wear through | of course he did. an eye opens, big as a shield, and he runs all the way home to vasudheim
D: and in every version he swears the ribbon still held. the one detail that never changes | the one thing he never changes when he tells it: the chain held
~ 15
B: i heard he keeps a thread of it in his pack and won't show anyone | the way i heard it, he still has one thread of the ribbon and changes the subject when you ask
C: now i have to go hear it myself | i'm going to vasudheim to hear him tell it
D: bring coin. the good ending comes after the third ale | bring coin. the best part costs three ales

